{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"edits\":[{\"path\":\"summary/text\",\"value_json\":\"杯 means “cup” or “drinking vessel.” A common analysis treats 木 as a meaning component and 不 as a proposed sound component; a separate analysis of related 桮 names 否. The accounts do not settle the earliest form.\"},{\"path\":\"summary/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref002\\\",\\\"ref010\\\",\\\"ref011\\\",\\\"ref014\\\",\\\"ref030\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"formation/text\",\"value_json\":\"杯 is analyzed as a phonosemantic compound: 木 contributes meaning and 不 is proposed to cue the sound. The received analysis of related 桮 instead gives 木 plus 否 as its sound component. The Warring States analysis supports the 木 + 不 account for those forms, but the earliest form remains unresolved.\"},{\"path\":\"formation/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref002\\\",\\\"ref010\\\",\\\"ref014\\\",\\\"ref030\\\",\\\"ref034\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"components/0/text\",\"value_json\":\"木 is identified as the meaning component in analyses of 杯. Warring States forms are described as having 木 on the meaning side; the specific link between wood and the vessel meaning is not explained.\"},{\"path\":\"components/0/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref002\\\",\\\"ref014\\\",\\\"ref030\\\",\\\"ref034\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"components/1/text\",\"value_json\":\"不 is proposed as the sound component of 杯. In Zhengzhang’s Old Chinese reconstruction, 不 and 杯 share an initial and rhyme nucleus but differ in the reconstructed lateral and vowel length; this supports a sound-series relation, not proof of the earliest form.\"},{\"path\":\"components/1/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref014\\\",\\\"ref020\\\",\\\"ref030\\\",\\\"ref037\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"history/1/text\",\"value_json\":\"A separate analysis treats 杯 as 木 + 不; the Warring States account describes 不 as the sound element and some short strokes as decorative. A scholarly proposal instead links 不 to a remnant of a hollowed tree. These accounts do not settle 不’s role in the earliest form or establish a specific graphic change.\"},{\"path\":\"history/1/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref013\\\",\\\"ref014\\\",\\\"ref020\\\",\\\"ref030\\\",\\\"ref035\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"relationships/0/text\",\"value_json\":\"In the proposed 木 + 不 analysis of 杯, 木 is identified as the meaning component; the Warring States account describes it as the meaning side, without specifying its contribution to the vessel.\"},{\"path\":\"relationships/0/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref002\\\",\\\"ref014\\\",\\\"ref030\\\",\\\"ref034\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"relationships/1/text\",\"value_json\":\"The Warring States analysis treats 不 as the sound element in 杯. Zhengzhang’s reconstructions support a proposed sound-series relation, but the competing account and lack of early specimens leave its role in the earliest form unsettled.\"},{\"path\":\"relationships/1/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref014\\\",\\\"ref017\\\",\\\"ref020\\\",\\\"ref030\\\",\\\"ref037\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"learner/overview/text\",\"value_json\":\"杯 means “cup” or “drinking vessel.” A common analysis combines 木, a meaning component, with 不, a proposed sound component; the Warring States account supports that analysis. A separate received account of 桮 names 否, and the earliest form remains unsettled.\"},{\"path\":\"learner/overview/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref002\\\",\\\"ref010\\\",\\\"ref011\\\",\\\"ref014\\\",\\\"ref030\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"learner/components/0/text\",\"value_json\":\"木 is identified as the meaning side in analyses of 杯, including the Warring States account; its specific link to the cup meaning is not explained.\"},{\"path\":\"learner/components/0/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref002\\\",\\\"ref014\\\",\\\"ref030\\\",\\\"ref034\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"learner/components/1/text\",\"value_json\":\"不 is proposed as a sound component; the Warring States analysis supports this role. The sound-series comparison does not prove that 不 belonged to the earliest form.\"},{\"path\":\"learner/components/1/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref014\\\",\\\"ref017\\\",\\\"ref020\\\",\\\"ref030\\\",\\\"ref037\\\"]\"}]}"}}
